\subsection{Stackless Serialization Mechanics}
Because Telix constructs concurrent kernel tasks using stackless Rust \texttt{Future} continuations, an in-flight operation is represented in memory as an anonymous compiler-generated state machine enum.

To migrate an executing task across nodes:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item The origin node pauses polling on the task's root \texttt{Future}.
    \item The state machine structure (containing only active variable fields rather than unallocated stack frame space) is serialized.
    \item Associated memory handles are reassigned as remote hardware capability tokens.
    \item The target node resumes execution simply by calling \texttt{Future::poll()} on its local event loop.
\end{enumerate}
